        <h2>Summary / Description</h2>
        <div class="description">
          The Mir Blood Collection System provides all of the medical and related supplies required to collect blood samples in support of the metabolism discipline science experiments.  Flight and backup hardware for the Mir Blood Collection System consists of five parts:  (1) Large Blood Collection Kits, one (2) Blood Tube Kit, two (3) Blood Collection Belts (BCB), one (4) Metabolic Accessory Kit and six (5) Sharps Containers.
<p>
<li><p>(1) The Large Blood Collection Kit is designed to support the metabolic sessions where blood samples are to be collected.  Each kit contains the medical equipment and related supplies necessary for establishing and maintaining a peripheral venous catheter.  All glass components are wrapped with Teflon tape and stowed in foam to prevent breakage and retain glass pieces in the event of breakage.  Each kit is used specifically for metabolic discipline sessions and designed for one-time usage.  The kits are intended to be discarded after each blood collection session as their contents are consumed.  The Large Blood Collection Kit has a mass of approximately 2.5 kg.
<p>
</p><li><p>(2) The Blood Tube Kit contains blood tubes to collect blood samples from three crewmembers and has a mass of approximately 5.0 kg.  The kit is intended to be used the same days as the Large Blood Collection Kits.  The kit contains foam blocks and blood tubes required for each day.  Each blood tube is labeled with a crewmember designation, color code, the metabolic session and target time for the blood draws.  
<p>
</p><li><p>(3) The Blood Collection Belt (BCB) consists of a belt, trash bag assembly, and "fanny pack" and has a mass of approximately 0.6 kg.  The designated "operator" for the blood collection sessions wears the belt around the waist.  The BCB trash bag is used to dispose of non-sharp biohazardous waste and any other waste generated during the sessions.  The "fanny pack" holds any medical supplies the operator uses during blood collection.  
<p>
</p><li><p>(4) The Metabolic Accessory Kit contains spare trash bag liners for the BCB, gloves for use during blood collection sessions, log books as a contingency in the event of a Bar Code Reader (BCR) failure, as well as spare tourniquets, Vacutainer<sup>TM</sup> holders, and tubex injectors.  The kit also contains spare battery packs and the data transfer cable for the Bar Code Reader.  The Metabolic Accessory Kit has a mass of approximately 4.0 kg.
<p>
</p><li><p>(5) The Sharps Container is a cylindrical aluminum device used to safely dispose sharp medical objects; it has a safety latch on the lid through which the sharps are inserted but cannot exit.  The container has a mass of approximately 0.3 kg.<end></end></p></li>
        </div>

